  bootwright / add-ons info
      Describe one built-in package from the executable alone, with no context, file or
      network: its purpose, the capabilities it provides and requires, its OLM package and
      default catalog source, every configuration field with whether it is required and its
      default, the namespaces it may place Secrets in, the lookup that answers a channel and
      CSV, and a binding skeleton whose required values are <field> placeholders. An unknown
      name refuses and names add-ons list.

  Usage
    bootwright add-ons info [flags]

  Command flags
      --name  Select one built-in package by name (required)

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright add-ons info --name metallb
